# DRAW keymap preset: Illustrator  (SAFEST — only DRAW-free target keys remapped)
#
# Format: actionId keycode requireMods forbidMods [device button]
#   mods bits: 1=Ctrl 2=Shift 4=Alt.  Action ids: GUI/COMMAND.BM (CMD_init) / SHORTCUTS.md.
# Policy (Rick, "safest"): applied ONLY if the target key is UNBOUND in DRAW. Collisions
# are documented, not applied — decide them in PLANS/PRESETS-KEYMAP-DECISIONS.md.
#
# Illustrator is a VECTOR app — many tools (Pen, Anchor, Type on path, Artboard) have
# no raster equivalent in DRAW, so this preset is mostly informational.

# --- Safe remaps (target key free in DRAW: Ctrl+I/J/K/U/W) ---
# Illustrator's Ctrl+J = "Join" (paths) has no DRAW equivalent; no provably-safe row. (none)

# --- COLLISIONS / not-applicable (documented) --------------------------------
#   P   Pen (bezier)        -> DRAW P is Polygon; DRAW bezier is Q (closest)
#   A   Direct Selection    -> DRAW A is free but no direct-select concept
#   V   Selection           -> DRAW V is Move (closest)
#   T   Type                -> DRAW T is Text (match)
#   M   Rectangle           -> DRAW M is Marquee; DRAW Rect is R
#   L   Ellipse             -> DRAW L is Line; DRAW Ellipse is C
#   \   Line Segment        -> DRAW \ is bound (guide/other)
#   Z   Zoom                -> DRAW Z is Zoom (match)
#   Ctrl+J Join paths       -> no DRAW equivalent (Ctrl+J stays free)
